{
  "requirement": "`habeas::validate_repository(root)` MUST return a report with the number of discovered requirements, the number of evidence files, and all validation errors for the supplied project. Ordinary invalid evidence MUST be reported in that report; an inaccessible project root MUST return an I/O error.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: false.** The implementation looks correct, but no test covers the I/O-error half of the requirement, and that half is cheap to test.\n\n**What the implementation does**\n- `validate_repository` (src/evidence.rs:119-122) returns `io::Result<EvidenceReport>` by calling `inspect_repository(root)?.report`.\n- `inspect_repository_with_progress` starts with `fs::canonicalize(root)?`. A missing or unreadable root therefore returns an `io::Error`, which meets the \"inaccessible project root MUST return an I/O error\" obligation.\n- Ordinary problems are pushed into `errors` instead of propagating. These include workspace config errors, evidence file problems, orphan and missing evidence, definition errors and reference coverage.\n- `EvidenceReport` carries `requirements`, `evidence_files` and `errors`. These match the spec, and the `{impl}` markers on the struct, `validate_repository`, `inspect_repository` and `inspect_repository_with_progress` cover the implementation.\n- The report also has an `examples` count. The requirement does not mention it, though the example definitions in other requirements plausibly justify it.\n\n**Tests that exist**\n- Counts of requirements and evidence files are asserted in `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` (src/evidence.rs:1474) and the other `{test}`-marked tests.\n- Ordinary invalid evidence is collected into `report.errors` while the call still returns `Ok`. `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` (src/evidence.rs:1507) exercises many invalid-evidence cases.\n- The `{test}` markers in tests/commands.rs and tests/evidence_boundaries.rs also use the API successfully.\n\n**The gap**\n- I found no test, `{test}`-marked or otherwise, where `validate_repository` is called on a nonexistent or inaccessible root and the result is asserted to be `Err`. A search for `is_err`, `unwrap_err` and `NotFound` in tests and `src` found nothing for it.\n- The `{test}` references listed for this requirement cover only the `Ok` path.\n- The I/O-error obligation is a distinct MUST in the requirement. It is a distinct point in the design space, and a test for it would be only a few lines.\n- It is neither impractical nor so simple that omitting the test is justified.\n- No FIXME or issue reference acknowledges the gap.\n\nAdding a test that asserts an error for a nonexistent root, with `{test}` marked on it, would likely make this pass.",
  "inputs": [
